    {
      "name": "Table 2",
      "caption": "Segmentation performance. KFTT corpus (440k sentences) is used for evaluation. Experiments are executed on Linux with Xeon 3.5Ghz processors. The size of vocabulary is 16k. Moses and KyTea tokenizers are used for English and Japanese respectively. Note that we have to take the time of pre-tokenization into account to make a fair comparison with and without pre-tokenization. Because subword-nmt is based on BPE, we used the BPE model in SentencePiece. We found that BPE and unigram language models show almost comparable performance.",
      "label": "result2",
      "numericCells": 18,
